{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You were admitted this morning for worsening diarrhea and abdominal pain. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, thanks. So for the past few days, my bowel movements went from about 6 a day to every hour. They’re watery, yellow-green, no blood, but I’ve seen a little on the toilet paper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a low-grade fever, like 100.3, the morning before I came in. And my left lower belly pain is sharp and crampy. It’s worse now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You also mentioned pain in your left testicle and flank. Can you describe that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, the testicle pain started right before I came to the ER. It feels heavy, like a pulling. I only have one testicle—I had the left one removed years ago. And my back, left side, hurts too. I’ve had kidney stones before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for that. We’ll check for infection and inflammation. We’ve started IV fluids because your labs show mild dehydration and your kidney function is a bit off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my kidney okay? Last time I was in, my creatinine was high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is 1.3, up from your baseline of 1.1. But it’s likely due to dehydration from the diarrhea. We’re giving fluids, and it should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I’ve been on prednisone for years. Should I keep taking it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re actually increasing it to 40 mg daily because we suspect a Crohn’s flare. We’ve also started IV steroids and an antibiotic, ciprofloxacin, just in case there’s infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to Flagyl and Zofran. Are you using those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’re avoiding those. You’re on ciprofloxacin, which you’ve taken before without issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Also, I’ve been feeling pins and needles in my left foot and up to my knee. Started in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2178-08-05 06:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. It could be related to nerve irritation from the abdominal inflammation or part of your chronic back pain. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2178-08-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your stool tests came back negative for C. diff, Salmonella, Shigella, and parasites. No infection found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2178-08-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s definitely a flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2178-08-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely yes. Your CT scan shows thickening at the anastomosis site—consistent with Crohn’s flare. We also saw a small 2-mm kidney stone in your left kidney, but it’s not blocking anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2178-08-05 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could that be causing the back and testicle pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2178-08-05 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The stone might have passed and caused referred pain. Your scrotal ultrasound showed no torsion, but there is an enlarged vessel in the left groin. We’ll follow up on that with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2178-08-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really uncomfortable. Can I get something for pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2178-08-05 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re giving IV hydromorphone for now. We’ll adjust as your pain improves. We also restarted your quetiapine for anxiety—you weren’t taking it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2178-08-05 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forgot. I’ve been stressed. A close friend’s been going through a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2178-08-05 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. We’ll help manage your anxiety while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your MRI enterography confirms active Crohn’s disease in the distal ileum—about 7-8 cm of inflamed bowel. No abscess or complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So same as before. No surgery needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not at this time. Medication should control it. We’re planning a sigmoidoscopy tomorrow to get biopsies and confirm the flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to be sedated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be lightly sedated. It’s a short procedure. After that, we can start you on food again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hungry. Been on IV fluids too long."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2178-08-06 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. Once the scope is done and we confirm it’s safe, we’ll advance your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2178-08-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The sigmoidoscopy showed ulceration and inflammation at the anastomosis. Biopsies confirm active inflammation. No infection in the tissue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2178-08-07 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So definitely a flare. What’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2178-08-07 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you from IV to oral prednisone. You’ll continue 40 mg daily until you speak with your GI doctor. We’re also sending you home with a 10-day course of oral ciprofloxacin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2178-08-07 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2178-08-07 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re getting there. Your diarrhea has slowed, and you’re tolerating a regular diet. We’ll keep you one more day to make sure your pain is controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2178-08-07 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My back pain is still bothering me. Can I get something for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2178-08-07 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re prescribing a lidocaine patch and cyclobenzaprine for muscle spasms. Avoid driving or alcohol—they can make you drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2178-08-07 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already on tizanidine at night. Should I keep that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2178-08-07 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re stopping tizanidine because cyclobenzaprine is similar. Taking both could increase sedation. Use the new meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2178-08-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs today look better. White count is down, kidney function stable. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2178-08-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the pins and needles in my leg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2178-08-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still likely related to nerve irritation from the flare. It should improve as inflammation decreases. Let us know if it worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2178-08-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve noticed some scabs on my chest and tattoos. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2178-08-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw that. Probably minor skin irritation. We’re giving you bacitracin ointment to apply as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. Your symptoms have improved, and labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue prednisone 40 mg daily until you talk to your GI doctor—they’ll guide the taper. Take ciprofloxacin twice daily for 10 days. Use the lidocaine patch and cyclobenzaprine as needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the hydromorphone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take one tablet every 6 hours as needed for severe pain. Don’t exceed that. And call your PCP about the enlarged groin vessel seen on ultrasound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be on any infection prevention? I’m on a lot of steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. Discuss Bactrim prophylaxis with your doctor. It can help prevent infections when on long-term steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my B12 shot? I’m overdue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll schedule that with your PCP. Keep up with monthly injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll follow up with GI and my regular doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And if diarrhea worsens, fever returns, or pain increases, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I just want to feel normal again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on the right track. Keep hydrated, rest, and take your meds as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I avoid pork and broccoli? I ate those before this started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They might have triggered it. Stick to your usual diet for now and reintroduce foods slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2178-08-09 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you only if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2178-08-05 05:32:00",
    "admission_end": "2178-08-09 12:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of Crohn’s disease, status post colectomy and ileorectal anastomosis, long-term steroid use, and nephrolithiasis was admitted for increased diarrhea, abdominal pain, and new-onset left flank and testicular pain. Workup revealed a Crohn’s flare confirmed by CT, MRI enterography, and sigmoidoscopy with biopsy, showing inflammation at the anastomosis. A 2-mm non-obstructing kidney stone was noted, possibly contributing to referred pain. Infectious causes were ruled out. Acute kidney injury (creatinine 1.3 mg/dL) was attributed to dehydration and resolved with IV fluids. Pain was managed with IV hydromorphone, later transitioned to oral. The patient improved clinically, with diarrhea resolving to baseline and pain controlled. He was discharged home on prednisone 40 mg daily pending GI follow-up, a 10-day course of ciprofloxacin, cyclobenzaprine, lidocaine patch, and hydromorphone for breakthrough pain, with instructions to discontinue tizanidine and follow up on an incidental finding of an enlarged left groin vessel.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Unspecified hereditary and idiopathic peripheral neuropathy",
      "Intestinal bypass or anastomosis status",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids"
    ]
  }
}
